    <p class="section-number">01 · Commercial freezer not freezing</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Three root causes our techs diagnose first across LA commercial kitchens.</h2>

    <p>A commercial freezer that won't hold 0°F or below — USDA federal frozen storage threshold — usually traces to one of three root causes our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair diagnose first across LA County restaurant, hotel, grocery, and hospitality operations. (1) Defrost system failure — defrost timer ($280 to $440) not initiating cycle, defrost heater ($380 to $580) open circuit, or snap-disc defrost termination thermostat stuck. The evaporator coil becomes a block of ice over 24 to 72 hours and stops transferring heat into the refrigerant. About 30 to 35 percent of "not freezing" calls. (2) Dirty condenser coil — grease, lint, and dust accumulate on the condenser fins, head pressure climbs, cooling capacity drops. About 20 to 25 percent resolve at the $120 commercial diagnostic with condenser cleaning, no parts charge. (3) Compressor failure year 7 to 10 typical wear curve — compressor runs continuously but box won't reach 0°F, or compressor short-cycles, or audible knocking. $1,400 to $2,200 reach-in scale, $1,800 to $3,200 walk-in scale, $2,200 to $3,600 two-stage compressor systems.</p>

    <p>This page covers commercial freezer not-freezing diagnostic across all seven Southern California counties — Sunset Strip restaurants, DTLA hotel banquet kitchens prepping evening service, Beverly Hills hospitality, Long Beach port-adjacent food service and cold-chain logistics, Pasadena specialty grocery, Inland Empire commercial kitchens in Ontario warehouses, and LA ice cream and frozen dessert operations. Every hour of commercial freezer downtime equals real inventory loss exposure and federal USDA frozen storage compliance pressure.</p>

    <p><strong>$120 commercial diagnostic, applied toward repair.</strong> BHGS Registration #A49573 and EPA 608 Universal certified (#1346255700410), plus R-290 propane certification for newer green-refrigerant commercial freezers. CSLB C-20 HVAC. BBB Accredited Business. 90-day warranty. Same-day across LA, OC, Ventura. Next-day Riverside and San Bernardino. Sister sub-services: <a href="/commercial/refrigeration/walk-in-cooler-not-cooling/">walk-in cooler not cooling</a>, <a href="/commercial/refrigeration/walk-in-freezer-repair/">walk-in freezer repair pillar</a>, <a href="/commercial/refrigeration/reach-in-freezer-repair/">reach-in freezer repair</a>, <a href="/commercial/refrigeration/compressor-issues/">compressor issues</a>, <a href="/commercial/refrigeration/not-cooling/">generic commercial refrigeration not cooling</a>. Parent: <a href="/commercial/refrigeration/">commercial refrigeration</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 02 DIAGNOSTIC SEQUENCE -->
<section class="section section-gray">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">02 · Five-step diagnostic on every commercial freezer not-freezing call</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Cheap-first sequence. Most calls resolve before sealed-system work.</h2>

    <ol class="num-list">
      <li><strong>Box temperature documentation.</strong> Probe at product level (not air space at ceiling) to verify current product temperature against the operator's last log entry. Establishes USDA federal frozen storage compliance window and HACCP CCP exceedance documentation for California Retail Food Code.</li>
      <li><strong>Visual evaporator coil inspection.</strong> Ice formation indicates defrost system failure (timer, heater, or snap-disc termination thermostat). Heavy frost coverage indicates door gasket leak or excessive door openings. Photo documentation for the operator's HACCP records.</li>
      <li><strong>Visual condenser inspection.</strong> Restaurant kitchen grease, dust, lint accumulation on fins. If condenser is the diagnosis, cleaning runs $200 to $280 and resolves the call without parts on roughly 20 to 25 percent of LA commercial freezer service visits.</li>
      <li><strong>Compressor amp draw and head pressure measurement.</strong> Multimeter at compressor terminals against data plate spec, manifold gauges on high and low side. Two-stage compressor verification on low-temperature applications — stuck in low-stage equals chronic warm freezer. Out-of-spec readings narrow to sealed-system versus mechanical compressor wear.</li>
      <li><strong>Door gasket plus door switch verification.</strong> Air infiltration at gasket allows warm humid LA kitchen air into the box, defrost cycle overwhelmed by moisture load. Door switch stuck closed keeps interior light running, heat load on refrigeration system.</li>
    </ol>

    <p>Most diagnostics complete in 25 to 40 minutes on-site. Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair walk operators through the findings with photo documentation before any repair work begins. Sealed-system work (refrigerant leak, TXV, compressor) requires EPA 608 Universal certification (#1346255700410) plus R-290 certification for newer green-refrigerant models, which we hold and document on every commercial freezer service visit.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 03 TOP CAUSES FREQUENCY -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">03 · Top causes by frequency</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Across LA County commercial freezer not-freezing calls.</h2>

    <p>Across LA County commercial freezer service calls our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair run — Sunset Strip restaurants running 14 to 18 hour kitchen shifts seven days a week, DTLA hotel banquet kitchens prepping 200-plate evening service, Beverly Hills luxury hospitality, Long Beach port-adjacent cold-chain logistics, Pasadena specialty grocery, Inland Empire commercial kitchens in Ontario warehouses, and LA ice cream and frozen dessert operations — the failure breakdown clusters predictably.</p>

    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>1. Defrost system failure (30-35% of calls)</h3>
      <p>Most common single root cause across LA commercial freezer service. Standard mechanical defrost timer initiates a heating cycle every 6 to 8 hours; when the timer fails ($280 to $440), the defrost heater open-circuits ($380 to $580), or the snap-disc termination thermostat sticks, frost accumulates on the evaporator until the coil becomes a block of ice. Walk-in freezer scale typically more severe than reach-in because lower operating temperature accelerates frost formation between cycles. Our techs clear ice at the visit (60 to 90 minutes manual plus warm-water defrost) and replace failed component same-day from truck stock for common Paragon, Intermatic, and Grasslin defrost timer brands.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>2. Dirty condenser coil (20-25% of calls)</h3>
      <p>Restaurant kitchen grease, dust, lint accumulate on condenser fins. Heat can't dissipate efficiently, head pressure climbs, cooling capacity drops, box temperature drifts up. About 20 to 25 percent of all commercial freezer not-freezing calls resolve at the $120 commercial diagnostic with condenser cleaning, no parts charge. Standalone deep cleaning runs $200 to $280.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>3. Evaporator fan motor failure (15-20% of calls)</h3>
      <p>Year 5 to 9 typical wear curve. No airflow across the evaporator coil, cold air doesn't circulate through the box, product near the coil stays frozen while product near the door warms above 0°F. Customer reports zones of frozen and warm within the same unit. $320 to $520 replacement, same-day from truck stock for common shaded-pole motor sizes.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>4. Refrigerant leak (10-15% of calls)</h3>
      <p>Suction line or evaporator inlet pinhole, joint failure, vibration fatigue at copper fittings. Symptom: gradual loss of cooling capacity over weeks, frost line shifts on suction line, head pressure low. Requires EPA 608 Universal certified work — leak detection (electronic sniffer, UV dye where applicable), evacuation to deep vacuum, recharge with correct refrigerant (R-404A commercial standard, R-448A or R-449A transitional, R-290 propane on newer green models, R-454A post-2024). $700 to $1,500 typical all-in.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>5. Compressor failure (8-12% of calls)</h3>
      <p>Year 7 to 10 typical wear curve. Compressor runs continuously without bringing box to 0°F, or short-cycles, or audible knocking. Two-stage compressors used on lower-temperature freezer applications (Copeland, Tecumseh) wear faster than single-stage refrigerator equivalents. $1,400 to $2,200 reach-in scale, $1,800 to $3,200 walk-in scale, $2,200 to $3,600 two-stage systems, all-in including EPA 608 refrigerant recovery and recharge.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>6. Door gasket, door switch, TXV (5-10% of calls)</h3>
      <p>Door gasket warm humid LA kitchen air infiltration $180 to $340 replacement plus deep frost clear. Door switch stuck closed keeping interior light as heat load $80 to $160. TXV (thermostatic expansion valve) failure year 8 to 12 $480 to $680. Combined these resolve the remaining 5 to 10 percent of commercial freezer not-freezing calls.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

